# Reviewed exceptions to the citation-frame advisory (trace.py, warn-only).
#
# One entry per line: `<ROW-ID> <Cell> <token>`, then ` — OI-###: <reason>`.
# A line with no ` — ` separator, or with fewer than three fields before it,
# declares NOTHING and is dropped.
#
# THE `OI-###` IS REQUIRED, AND IT IS THE FIRST TOKEN OF THE REASON (OI-41 ARM 1,
# ruled 2026-08-20 — hard at birth). An exception is a DEFERRED DECISION: the
# entry says a rule this repo mechanizes is knowingly not satisfied, so it must
# NAME the open-items row that carries the question. An entry with no id, or one
# naming a row `docs/requirements/open-items.toml` does not have, is an INTEGRITY
# finding on the always-on `--strict-integrity` floor — a field, so it has no
# false positives, and the bad state is unrepresentable rather than merely
# detected. The 19 entries this replaced said the same thing in prose ("owes an
# open-item row at the sitting"), nineteen times, and produced zero rows: the
# announcement and the queue were two unconnected artifacts. Position, not
# mention — an id further into the sentence is prose, not the field.
#
# TOKEN-SCOPED, and that is the whole design. An entry silences the ONE token it
# names — spelled as the finding reports it, whitespace-collapsed and
# case-insensitive — never the cell around it. The earlier row/cell key was
# measured wrong on 2026-08-18: 15 entries here read "unsigned derived-requirement
# label", which is one parenthetical, while suppressing every frame in the same
# `Rationale`; re-running detection with the list ignored exposed 67 tokens over
# 22 rows that nobody had adjudicated, `RE-VOICED 2026-08-17` and
# `Minted at the owner's 2026-08-15` among them — the banned shape itself, riding
# a carve-out written for a label. So a frame beside an allowed one still
# reports, and re-wording an allowed cell re-opens the question rather than
# laundering a new frame through an old entry.
#
# THIS FILE IS NOT A SECOND HOME FOR PROVENANCE. Every entry below is one shape:
# the token is the ONLY record that a question is OPEN — a contradiction between
# two rows, an obligation whose carrier is gone, a label nothing mechanical
# signs. Stripping those would delete the repo's only note that the question is
# unresolved, which is worse than the frame. Each row below NAMES the open-item
# row its question sits in; when that ruling's execution lands, the token leaves
# the cell and the entry goes with it (a dead entry fails tests/test_trace.py).
#
# THE HELD POPULATION THIS FILE CANNOT LIST — the IF `Contract` cells, ruled
# 2026-08-19 (OI-36, option (b)). 49 findings from a DIFFERENT detector
# (`trace.if_contract_advisories`: 46 `Contract names WI-###`, 3 `Contract cites
# decision`) are deliberately NOT swept under the provenance rule, and they get
# no entries below because that detector takes no `allow` parameter at all — an
# entry naming them would declare nothing and silence nothing. The hold is
# recorded HERE, on the surface a reader meets, rather than in a log fragment,
# which was the whole finding: the exclusion had been resting on one sentence
# that nothing pinned, so a population of 49 could grow or shrink with no
# artifact changing and no one told.
#
# WHAT THE HOLD IS WAITING ON, named so it can expire rather than drift: WI-455's
# interface lane rewrites those `Contract` cells for other reasons, and its
# remainder is itself blocked behind WI-469 (`Consumes` rows that name the
# medium). Sweeping the 49 now would drive a prose campaign through 46 cells that
# lane is about to re-author — one pass instead of two is the entire argument. If
# WI-469 is abandoned or the chain outlives the interface lane, this clause is the
# thing to re-open: the hold is bounded by those two work items and by nothing
# else. The eight citation FRAMES that were the other half of OI-36 are swept, so
# the frame detector reports zero and this file's entries are the only exceptions.

